  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aria&#x2019;s story is one of resilience and justice. With support from Femili PNG, Aria*, a woman with disability, fought to protect herself and her daughters from ongoing threats, intimidation and social exclusion. When Aria learned the girls&apos; father was abusing the children, she took steps, and helped to break the silence on social stigma in the community. She reported to the Family Support Centre and police. It was the first time a woman in her village reported. Aria worried about the risk of social isolation/retaliation from her former partner&apos;s family/community. Police arrested him but in the 3 years to bring charges agianats him, Aria was accused of fabrication and faced mounting threats and intimidation from the father&#x2019;s relatives. To keep them safe, Femili PNG provided temporary safe accommodation, emotional and psychological support, and case management support. The court found the father guilty and is serving a long jail sentence. With Femili and police assistance Aria and her daughters were successfully reintegrated into a safe and welcoming community. Aria is an advocate for survivors - her courage has inspired other women to seek help and break the cycle of violence.
&#x200d;
*Not her real name. Identity withheld to protect privacy.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, the PNG Women&#x2019;s Business Resource Centre piloted the &#x201c;Pay-It-Forward Loan&#x201d; (PIF) initiatives providing women entrepreneurs with small scale funding for business start-ups. 24 women were provided loans to support their businesses. They then &apos;paid forward&#x2019; the zero-interest loans to other women entrepreneurs through donations of products or services, coaching and mentorship, or income generation training to vulnerable community members.  As a result of the pilot, 392 women&#x2019;s SMEs from 9 provinces were positively impacted. By supporting women entrepreneurs, the pilot fostered a sense of communal responsibility, where individual success was shared and multiplied across communities. Michelle Ososo used a PIF Loan to establish a small fish market and purchase a dinghy to catch fresh fish to sell. Michelle repaid her loans by providing in-kind donations to a Tami women&#x2019;s group including bilums, basket weaving items, and sustainable livelihoods training for 45 women.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
